From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wize-logic <wizelogic@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:26:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] recomp: --x87-locals keeps a function's x87 stack in C locals

The x87 stack is modelled in memory: g_fp_stack[8] and its index
g_fp_top, through fp_push, fp_pop, fp_top and fp_st, beside the control
word and the last compare in g_fp_control_word, g_fp_cmp and g_fp_cc.
That state has to be in memory where control crosses a function boundary
(st(0) carries arguments and results, and one guest routine can lift to
several C functions), but inside a body every operation then reloads the
index, computes an address, loads or stores a double and reads the
control word again for RECOMP_FP_PC. On a PowerPC host that is most of
the time of x87-heavy code.

With --x87-locals, translate_function hands each function that uses the
x87 to x87_locals.py, which works on the C text it emitted. At each
statement either memory is the truth (on entry, after a call) or locals
are:

- the first x87 statement after memory was the truth loads a base index
  from g_fp_top, the control word, the compare results and the stack
  positions the function uses; st(i) at static depth k (values pushed
  since) is position i - k, a double local, so fp_push, fp_pop and fp_st
  become assignments, nothing and names, and RECOMP_FP_PC becomes
  RECOMP_FP_PC_CW(local, x);
- before every statement that calls out or leaves (a guest call, a tail
  call, RECOMP_ICALL*, RECOMP_ITAIL, a return, any name it does not know)
  the positions written that still hold a value, g_fp_top when the depth
  moved and the changed scalars are stored; memory is the truth after it,
  so a callee that returns a value in st(0), pops an argument or changes
  the control word is seen by the next load;
- where paths join, the edges are made to agree: an edge from memory
  loads (in a block of its own on a goto, so only that path pays), locals
  that hold nothing new join memory for free, and a label reached at
  different depths (after a call that left a value on one path only) is
  entered through memory, its edges with locals writing them back;
- the same expressions compute the same doubles, so results are
  identical. Wherever memory is the truth it holds what the memory model
  holds there, in every slot from st(0) down; the empty slots above st(0)
  may keep an older value than the memory model's last popped one, and
  no x87 instruction can read them.

The analysis is a dataflow over the function's own C statements: a goto
is an edge, an unconditional goto or return ends one, and nothing else
reaches a label (no label addresses are taken), so it guesses nothing
about the x86 code. A statement it cannot rewrite, and a conditional or
loop written over several lines, runs on memory. A function keeps the
memory model when it uses more than eight positions, has a goto in a
statement that calls out, or calls setjmp. RECOMP_BACKEDGE is taken not
to touch the x87 state: a runtime whose safe point switches guest threads
or runs interrupt work must save and restore the x87 registers around it,
as it must the others.

The option is off by default. The template header gains RECOMP_FP_PC_CW
(RECOMP_FP_PC is that with g_fp_control_word).
